---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import site from '../../site.config.json' with { type: 'json' };

const page = {
  url: '/disclaimer/', title: 'Important Information Disclaimer',
  seoTitle: 'Marine Diesel Information Disclaimer', pageType: 'legal',
  status: 'ready', author: site.defaultAuthor, reviewer: null,
  needsReviewer: false, parent: '/', parentTitle: 'Home',
  schema: ['WebPage', 'BreadcrumbList'], updated: site.legalUpdated,
  indexable: true, blockers: [], headings: [], faqs: [],
  description: 'Important limits of the marine diesel information on this site. Advice can be incomplete, out of date or wrong for your vessel.',
};
---
<Page page={page}>
  <h1>Information disclaimer</h1>
  <p>
    This site provides general educational information about marine diesel
    engines. It is not a diagnosis, a repair instruction for your particular
    vessel, or a substitute for inspection by a qualified marine professional.
  </p>

  <section class="safety" role="note">
    <h2>The advice can be wrong</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Information on this site can be incomplete, out of date,
      misunderstood or simply wrong.</strong> Engines with similar symptoms can
      have different faults. Model changes, previous repairs, non-standard
      installations and the condition of your vessel can make a generally
      sensible step unsafe in your case.
    </p>
    <p>
      Never use this site as the only basis for a decision involving fire,
      flooding, fuel, electrical isolation, loss of propulsion or safety at sea.
    </p>
  </section>

  <h2>Stop when safety is uncertain</h2>
  <p>
    Shut the engine down when a guide says to do so, when an alarm sounds, when
    cooling water stops, or whenever continued operation may cause harm. If you
    are underway, put the safety of the people and vessel first and follow your
    emergency procedures. Contact the appropriate emergency or marine rescue
    service where necessary.
  </p>

  <h2>Use the correct manufacturer information</h2>
  <p>
    The operator, workshop and installation manuals for your exact engine,
    gearbox and vessel take priority over a general article. Confirm the model,
    serial number and installation before ordering parts, selecting fluids,
    applying torque values or opening a fuel, cooling or electrical system.
    Our <a href="/resources/">authority resources</a> page explains where to
    find primary sources.
  </p>

  <h2>No professional relationship</h2>
  <p>
    Reading this site or contacting us does not create a mechanic–customer,
    engineer–client, surveyor–client or other professional relationship. We do
    not inspect your vessel, verify the facts you provide or supervise work.
  </p>

  <h2>Prices, listings and external links</h2>
  <p>
    Costs are indicative and may change. Business listings are not endorsements,
    and you must confirm licences, insurance, experience and availability
    directly. External sites can change without notice and remain responsible
    for their own information.
  </p>

  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>
    If you find an error, please <a href="/contact/">tell us</a>. Include the
    page address, the statement in question and, where possible, a primary
    source such as a current manufacturer manual or government publication.
  </p>
</Page>
